<%# How many characters the question may still take before the server refuses
    it (LegalChatbotService::MAX_QUESTION_LENGTH, carried as data-max). The
    count is written and kept by services/chatbot_question_length.js, which
    measures as the server does; it turns amber near the end and red past it,
    and Send is refused while it is red. The visible count is aria-hidden: the
    box points at it with aria-describedby, and the status beside it speaks
    once typing pauses.
    Locals: id (the box's aria-describedby), controller (the Stimulus
    identifier that owns the box), size_class (optional). %>
<% size_class = local_assigns.fetch(:size_class, 'text-[11px]') %>
<div class="mt-1 flex justify-end">
  <span id="<%= id %>"
        data-<%= controller %>-target="questionCount"
        data-max="<%= LegalChatbotService::MAX_QUESTION_LENGTH %>"
        data-state="ok"
        aria-hidden="true"
        class="min-h-4 <%= size_class %> leading-4 tabular-nums text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 data-[state=warning]:text-amber-700 dark:data-[state=warning]:text-amber-300 data-[state=over]:font-semibold data-[state=over]:text-red-600 dark:data-[state=over]:text-red-400"></span>
  <span data-<%= controller %>-target="questionCountStatus" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
</div>
